# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Evaluation corpus build output (scripts/build_eval_corpus.py)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ingested corpora and raw filings are large (1.2 GB for eight 10-Ks) and fully
# regenerable: provenance.json carries every filing URL plus its SHA-256, and the
# corpus is a deterministic function of those filings and the pipeline config.
#
# queries.json and provenance.json are NOT ignored — together they are the dataset
# definition, and a query set that lives only on one machine cannot be evaluated
# against by anyone else.
# This is an allowlist, not a denylist, on purpose: the previous rule was
# `data/eval*/corpus/`, which matched data/eval/corpus/ but not the second corpus at
# data/eval/corpus_no_layout/, so 3.3 GB of build output was committed and GitHub
# rejected the push. Naming what may be committed cannot miss a new directory name.
data/*
!data/eval*/
data/eval*/*
!data/eval*/queries.json
!data/eval*/filings/
data/eval*/filings/*
!data/eval*/filings/provenance.json
